{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963583,"nonce":"LGIEnmR6qAUjLxZ4VnJpsNPvap8=","title":"Interface fat pointers reach erased T and Dynamic without being unwrapped","message":"Rows: Issue8528, TestInterface, Issue4363.\n\nAn interface value is a fresh heap fat pointer `[obj][slots..]` per class-\u003einterface conversion.\n`==` now compares by the wrapped object (haxe_iface_identity), but the fat pointer still escapes\nas-is into:\n\n- an erased `T` (`eq\u003cT\u003e(i, i.foo())`): compared and printed as a raw word; prints `\u003cunknown type N\u003e`\n  (the low 32 bits of `obj` read as a header);\n- Dynamic (`(px:Dynamic).getX()` in TestInterface): by-name dispatch reads the fat pointer as an\n  object and jumps to garbage (SIGSEGV).\n\nConverting an interface value to T or Dynamic should hand over the object (word 0); converting back\nto an interface rebuilds the fat pointer (`haxe_iface_fat_ptr_build`).","files":null}]}